Subject: [ReXGlue] merge s7/submitfix

Class: RGF
What: Failed async submissions / presenter fence signals can no longer hang a later wait (retry with backoff, then signal).
Evidence: Review finding on our own async submit path (PLAYBOOK Session 7).
On / off: Always on (error paths).
Commit: fdde345 (diff against fdde345^1)
Prepared by the WWE 2K14 recomp project (Session 15, prep only, not sent). Measured on one PC (Ryzen 9 5950X, RTX 4090), Vulkan backend, one title.

diff --git a/include/rex/ui/vulkan/queue_submit_order.h b/include/rex/ui/vulkan/queue_submit_order.h
index a8f6e2e..346740a 100644
--- a/include/rex/ui/vulkan/queue_submit_order.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/vulkan/queue_submit_order.h
@@ -172,6 +172,10 @@ class VulkanQueueSubmitOrder {
     return failed_count;
   }
 
+  // wwe2k14 patch (Session 7, SUBMITFIX review): submitting thread, when it stops retrying: forgets the kept fence
+  // signals (those fences stay unsignaled, as before SUBMITFIX), so later signals are no longer held behind them.
+  void DropFailedFenceSignals() { fence_signals_failed_.clear(); }
+
   WaitStats TakeWaitStats() {
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
     WaitStats wait_stats = wait_stats_;
diff --git a/src/graphics/vulkan/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/vulkan/command_processor.cpp
